Hair is a 1979 musical anti-war comedy-drama film directed by Miloš Forman and adapted for the screen by
Michael Weller, based on the 1968 Broadway musical Hair: The American Tribal Love-Rock Musical.

11
01:13:56,666 --> 01:14:02,666
Set against the backdrop of the hippie counterculture of the Vietnam era, the film focuses on a Vietnam War
draftee who meets and befriends a "tribe" of hippies while en route to the army induction center.

12
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
The hippies and their leader introduce him to marijuana, LSD, and their
environment of unorthodox relationships and draft evasion.

13
01:27:23,333 --> 01:27:29,333
The film stars an ensemble cast including John Savage, Treat Williams, Beverly D'Angelo,
Annie Golden, Dorsey Wright, Don Dacus, Cheryl Barnes and Ronnie Dyson.

14
01:34:06,666 --> 01:34:12,666
Dance scenes were choreographed by Twyla Tharp and
were performed by Tharp's dancers.

15
01:40:50,000 --> 01:40:56,000
Hair was nominated for two Golden Globes: Best Motion Picture – Musical or
Comedy, and New Star of the Year in a Motion Picture (for Williams).

16
01:47:33,333 --> 01:47:39,333
The film explores themes of vietnam war, new york city, army, hippie, free love.

17
01:54:16,666 --> 01:54:22,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
